<h1>Using the iconvert class</h1>

<p>The <a href="../classes/html/classiconvert.html">iconvert class</a> implements a character encoding converter.</p>

<p>It can be used to convert strings between various character encodings, such as between char, wchar_t, and UCS-2, or between any encodings supported by the system's iconv implementation.</p>

<p>To convert between encodings, create an instance of iconvert, set the from and to encodings, set the from and to buffers and their sizes, and call convert().</p>

<p>The "from encoding" and "to encoding" use standard iconv encoding names.  An empty string for the encoding indicates the default system encoding.  "WCHAR_T" indicates the wchar_t encoding.  "UCS-2BE" and "UCS-2LE" indicate big-endian and little-endian UCS-2 encodings.</p>

